<title>POLAND: Polish cabinet body sets wage adjustment payout.</title>
<headline>Polish cabinet body sets wage adjustment payout.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish cabinet's Social Political Committee said on Wednesday that public sector workers whose income did not increase the planned 5.5 percent in real terms last year will get a one-off payment in February.</p>
<p>It said public sector workers would be given 16.3 zlotys on average from government reserves.</p>
<p>The Labour Ministry estimated the total cost of the payout at 210 million zlotys, PAP news agency reported.</p>
<p>Public sector workers were entitled to a wage increase of 5.5 percent above the planned 1996 inflation of 19.8 percent, but average year-on-year inflation was higher last year.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
